 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.52,
   "text": "What's the longest possible sunset you can experience while driving, assuming you're",
   "avg_logprob": -0.091,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 3.52,
   "end": 5.36,
   "text": "obeying the speed limit and driving on paved roads?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.091,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 5.86,
   "end": 9.56,
   "text": "For the purpose of our question, sunset starts the instant the sun touches the horizon and",
   "avg_logprob": -0.091,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 9.56,
   "end": 10.92,
   "text": "ends when it disappears completely.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.091,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 11.24,
   "end": 13.4,
   "text": "Which means that, for us, this is not a sunset.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.091,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 13.9,
   "end": 15.28,
   "text": "This is also not a sunset.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.091,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 15.74,
   "end": 17.28,
   "text": "This is definitely not a sunset.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.091,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 17.78,
   "end": 20.56,
   "text": "And no matter what happens here, this will not be a sunset.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.091,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 21.12,
   "end": 24.72,
   "text": "If the sun touches the horizon and then it lifts back up, the sunset is disqualified.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.091,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 25.38,
   "end": 28.8,
   "text": "For a sunset to count, the sun also can't just disappear behind a nearby hill.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.091,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 28.8,
   "end": 31.22,
   "text": "It needs to set behind the ideal ice horizon.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.175,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 31.6,
   "end": 34.74,
   "text": "At London's latitude, the Earth's surface is moving from west to east at about 1,000",
   "avg_logprob": -0.175,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 34.74,
   "end": 35.54,
   "text": "kilometers per hour.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.175,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 35.84,
   "end": 39.36,
   "text": "So if you fly west in a commercial airliner, you can experience an arbitrarily long sunset.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.175,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 39.72,
   "end": 42.58,
   "text": "Or at least, you can until you run out of fuel 15 or 20 hours in.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.175,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 43.1,
   "end": 46.54,
   "text": "Intuitively, it seems like we probably want to be as far north or maybe south as possible.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.175,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 46.82,
   "end": 49.44,
   "text": "The closer we are to the pole, the easier it is to keep up with the sun.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.175,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 50.04,
   "end": 52.88,
   "text": "Unfortunately, there are no paved roads anywhere near either pole.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.175,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 53.2,
   "end": 56.6,
   "text": "The closest road that qualifies is probably in Long Erebyen on the island of Svalbard,",
   "avg_logprob": -0.175,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 56.74,
   "end": 56.94,
   "text": "Norway.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.175,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 56.94,
   "end": 59.46,
   "text": "The longest sunset there lasts just under an hour.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.013
  },
  {
   "start": 59.86,
   "end": 62.48,
   "text": "In general, driving west to keep up with the sun isn't a viable strategy.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.013
  },
  {
   "start": 62.94,
   "end": 66.28,
   "text": "Even at the northernmost tip of mainland Norway, you'd have to travel at about half the",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.013
  },
  {
   "start": 66.28,
   "end": 67.96,
   "text": "speed of sound to keep up with the sun.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.013
  },
  {
   "start": 68.52,
   "end": 69.76,
   "text": "Luckily, there's a better approach.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.013
  },
  {
   "start": 70.2,
   "end": 73.52,
   "text": "If you're in northern Scandinavia on a day when the sun just barely sets and then",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.013
  },
  {
   "start": 73.52,
   "end": 79.08,
   "text": "rises again, the day-night line moves northwest, then slows, reverses, and heads back to",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.013
  },
  {
   "start": 79.08,
   "end": 79.52,
   "text": "the southwest.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.013
  },
  {
   "start": 80.1,
   "end": 82.0,
   "text": "To get a long sunset, the strategy is simple.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.013
  },
  {
   "start": 82.34,
   "end": 85.86,
   "text": "Sit in your car until the sun first touches the horizon, which means the day-night line",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.013
  },
  {
   "start": 85.86,
   "end": 86.72,
   "text": "is about to pass you.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.093
  },
  {
   "start": 86.9,
   "end": 90.62,
   "text": "Then drive north to stay a little ahead of the line as long as you can, which will keep",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.093
  },
  {
   "start": 90.62,
   "end": 91.76,
   "text": "the sun in the process of setting.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.093
  },
  {
   "start": 92.08,
   "end": 95.12,
   "text": "Then you turn and drive south across the line into nighttime.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.093
  },
  {
   "start": 95.62,
   "end": 99.94,
   "text": "I ran a search for long sunset driving paths using some PIE-FM code and GPS traces of",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.093
  },
  {
   "start": 99.94,
   "end": 103.2,
   "text": "Norwegian highways, and I found that the strategy works about equally well anywhere",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.093
  },
  {
   "start": 103.2,
   "end": 104.2,
   "text": "inside the Arctic Circle.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.093
  },
  {
   "start": 104.52,
   "end": 108.16,
   "text": "Over a wide range of routes and driving speeds, the longest sunset I could come up with",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.093
  },
  {
   "start": 108.16,
   "end": 111.76,
   "text": "was consistently about 95 minutes, which is about 40 minutes longer than the longest",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.093
  },
  {
   "start": 111.76,
   "end": 113.12,
   "text": "sunset you can get in Long Erebyen.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.093
  },
  {
   "start": 113.12,
   "end": 117.42,
   "text": "But if you are stuck on Svalbard and you want to make the sunset, or sunrise, last a little",
   "avg_logprob": -0.177,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.023
  },
  {
   "start": 117.42,
   "end": 121.94,
   "text": "longer, you can always try spinning counterclockwise so your angular momentum slows the earth's",
   "avg_logprob": -0.177,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.023
  },
  {
   "start": 121.94,
   "end": 122.24,
   "text": "rotation.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.177,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.023
  },
  {
   "start": 122.78,
   "end": 127.44,
   "text": "It's true that it will only add an imperceptibly small fraction of a nanosecond, but it might",
   "avg_logprob": -0.177,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.023
  },
  {
   "start": 127.44,
   "end": 127.96,
   "text": "be worth it.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.177,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.023
  }
 ],
